n every one of them to say unto him, Lord, is it I?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaAnd he answered and said, He that dippeth his hand with me in the dish, the same shall betray me.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThe Son of man goeth as it is written of him: but woe unto that man by whom the Son of man is betrayed! it had been good for that man if he had not been born.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙeThen Judas, which betrayed him, answered and said, Master, is it I? He said unto him, Thou hast said.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŒAnd as they were eating, Jesus took bread, and blessed it, and brake it, and gave it to the disciples, and said, Take, eat; this is my body.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVAnd he took the cup, and gave thanks, and gave it to them, saying, Drink ye all of it;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\for this is my blood of the new testament, which is shed for many for the remission of sins.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBut I say unto you, I will not drink henceforth of this fruit of the vine, until that day when I drink it new with you in my Father's kingdom.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse#¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙGAnd when they had sung an hymn, they went out into the mount of Olives.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ²Then saith Jesus unto them, All ye shall be offended because of me this night: for it is written, I will smite the shepherd, and the sheep of the flock shall be scattered abroad.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ>But after I am risen again, I will go before you into Galilee.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqPeter answered and said unto him, Though all men shall be offended because of thee, yet will I never be offended.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnJesus said unto him, Verily I say unto thee, That this night, before the cock crow, thou shalt deny me thrice.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsPeter said unto him, Though I should die with thee, yet will I not deny thee. Likewise also said all the disciples.¦layout ªlast_verse#…¤book'§chapter«first_verse$ªlast_verse.¦verses›„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‚Then cometh Jesus with them unto a place called Gethsemane, and saith unto the disciples, Sit ye here, while I go and pray yonder.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaAnd he took with him Peter and the two sons of Zebedee, and began to be sorrowful and very heavy.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙkThen saith he unto them, My soul is exceeding sorrowful, even unto death: tarry ye here, and watch with me.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ°And he went a little further, and fell on his face, and prayed, saying, O my Father, if it be possible, let this cup pass from me: nevertheless not as I will, but as thou wilt.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{And he cometh unto the disciples, and findeth them asleep, and saith unto Peter, What, could ye not watch with me one hour?¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙgWatch and pray, that ye enter not into temptation: the spirit indeed is willing, but the flesh is weak.¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHe went away again the second time, and prayed, saying, O my Father, if this cup may not pass away from me, except I drink it, thy will be done.¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙCAnd he came and found them asleep again: for their eyes were heavy.¦layout ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙXAnd he left them, and went away again, and prayed the third time, saying the same words.¦layout ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ®Then cometh he to his disciples, and saith unto them, Sleep on now, and take your rest: behold, the hour is at hand, and the Son of man is betrayed into the hands of sinners.¦layout ªlast_verse-„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙARise, let us be going: behold, he is at hand that doth betray me.¦layout ªlast_verse.…¤book'§chapter«first_verse/ªlast_verse8¦versesš„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ£And while he yet spake, lo, Judas, one of the twelve, came, and with him a great multitude with swords and staves, from the chief priests and elders of the people.¦layout ªlast_verse/„¥verse0¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙkNow he that betrayed him gave them a sign, saying, Whomsoever I shall kiss, that same is he: hold him fast.¦layout ªlast_verse0„¥verse1¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙGAnd forthwith he came to Jesus, and said, Hail, master; and kissed him.¦layout ªlast_verse1„¥verse2¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpAnd Jesus said unto him, Friend, wherefore art thou come? Then came they, and laid hands on Jesus, and took him.¦layout ªlast_verse2„¥verse3¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙœAnd, behold, one of them which were with Jesus stretched out his hand, and drew his sword, and struck a servant of the high priest's, and smote off his ear.¦layout ªlast_verse3„¥verse4¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ~Then said Jesus unto him, Put up again thy sword into his place: for all they that take the sword shall perish with the sword.¦layout ªlast_verse4„¥verse5¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙuThinkest thou that I cannot now pray to my Father, and he shall presently give me more than twelve legions of angels?¦layout ªlast_verse5„¥verse6¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙEBut how then shall the scriptures be fulfilled, that thus it must be?¦layout ªlast_verse6„¥verse7¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÁIn that same hour said Jesus to the multitudes, Are ye come out as against a thief with swords and staves for to take me? I sat daily with you teaching in the temple, and ye laid no hold on me.¦layout ªlast_verse7„¥verse8¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|But all this was done, that the scriptures of the prophets might be fulfilled. Then all the disciples forsook him, and fled.¦layout ªlast_verse8…¤book'§chapter«first_verse9ªlast_verseD¦versesœ„¥verse9¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd they that had laid hold on Jesus led him away to Caiaphas the high priest, where the scribes and the elders were assembled.¦layout ªlast_verse9„¥verse:¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvBut Peter followed him afar off unto the high priest's palace, and went in, and sat with the servants, to see the end.¦layout ªlast_verse:„¥verse;¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpNow the chief priests, and elders, and all the council, sought false witness against Jesus, to put him to death;¦layout ªlast_verse;„¥verse<¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqbut found none: yea, though many false witnesses came, yet found they none. At the last came two false witnesses,¦layout ªlast_verse<„¥verse=¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙband said, This fellow said, I am able to destroy the temple of God, and to build it in three days.¦layout ªlast_verse=„¥verse>¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrAnd the high priest arose, and said unto him, Answerest thou nothing? what is it which these witness against thee?¦layout ªlast_verse>„¥verse?¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¨But Jesus held his peace. And the high priest answered and said unto him, I adjure thee by the living God, that thou tell us whether thou be the Christ, the Son of God.¦layout ªlast_verse?„¥verse@¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ°Jesus saith unto him, Thou hast said: nevertheless I say unto you, Hereafter shall ye see the Son of man sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven.¦layout ªlast_verse@„¥verseA¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ™Then the high priest rent his clothes, saying, He hath spoken blasphemy; what further need have we of witnesses? behold, now ye have heard his blasphemy.¦layout ªlast_verseA„¥verseB¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ=What think ye? They answered and said, He is guilty of death.¦layout ªlast_verseB„¥verseC¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙeThen did they spit in his face, and buffeted him; and others smote him with the palms of their hands,¦layout ªlast_verseC„¥verseD¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAsaying, Prophesy unto us, thou Christ, Who is he that smote thee?¦layout ªlast_verseD…¤book'§chapter«first_verseEªlast_verseK¦verses—„¥verseE¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnNow Peter sat without in the palace: and a damsel came unto him, saying, Thou also wast with Jesus of Galilee.¦layout ªlast_verseE„¥verseF¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙCBut he denied before them all, saying, I know not what thou sayest.¦layout ªlast_verseF„¥verseG¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd when he was gone out into the porch, another maid saw him, and said unto them that were there, This fellow was also with Jesus of Nazareth.¦layout ªlast_verseG„¥verseH¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ8And again he denied with an oath, I do not know the man.¦layout ªlast_verseH„¥verseI¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡And after a while came unto him they that stood by, and said to Peter, Surely thou also art one of them; for thy speech bewrayeth thee.¦layout ªlast_verseI„¥verseJ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_Then began he to curse and to swear, saying, I know not the man. And immediately the cock crew.¦layout ªlast_verseJ„¥verseK¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‘And Peter remembered the word of Jesus, which said unto him, Before the cock crow, thou shalt deny me thrice. And he went out, and wept bitterly.¦layout ªlast_verseK